# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines.
# The supervisor reads its stand-in counts before any child runs; a
# count is at its limit, so it enters the fail-safe state, stopping every
# child it does not keep - unnamed_child too, which its program does not
# name; the kept child runs, faults, and is stopped and reported, and
# nothing is reset. The "fault detail" line is not checked.
# The six failsafe-* expect files differ only in the two lines on the counts.
NOWAYOS: supervisor: starting; children kept_child (0) and stopped_child (1)
NOWAYOS: supervisor: counts read from the test stand-in, which stores nothing: restart count 4, sensitive count 0
NOWAYOS: supervisor: this start: a reset whose cause was not written down
NOWAYOS: supervisor: restart count 5 of 4, sensitive count 0 of 2: enter the fail-safe state
NOWAYOS: supervisor: stopped_child (1) stopped
NOWAYOS: supervisor: an unknown child (2) stopped
NOWAYOS: supervisor: in the fail-safe state; kept running: kept_child (0)
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: kept_child starting
NOWAYOS: supervisor: kept_child stopped: data write at 0x40000000: permission fault (the mapping does not allow it)
NOWAYOS: supervisor: in the fail-safe state: nothing is restarted

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match):
# a child it does not keep starting, the board reset, the reset returning, a
# fault the monitor had to handle, a kernel error message, or the supervisor
# or a probe failing.
!stopped_child starting
!unnamed_child starting
!resetting the board
!the reset returned
!NOT stopped
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!ISOLATION FAILURE
!no probe is defined
!no children are defined
!cannot stop
!cannot supervise
!cannot keep
